# ##  CHECK THE MODE CHANNEL FIRST.  ##
#
# If channel 5 has no travel -- no switch assigned on the transmitter -- the
# aircraft is not "stuck without mode switching", it is locked to whichever
# slot the channel's resting PWM selects. On this airframe RC5 sat at 1556,
# which ArduCopter's readSwitch() maps to slot 4. Apply this profile in that
# state and you are locked in ALT_HOLD, which is a worse first-flight mode than
# STABILIZE and needs a healthy barometer.
#
# Assign a switch to channel 5, run calibrate_radio.py --write, and confirm the
# mode name changes in MAVProxy as you flick it. Then apply this.
#
# A safe six-position flight mode set.
#
# ArduCopter 3.2.1 mode numbers:
#   0 STABILIZE   1 ACRO      2 ALT_HOLD   3 AUTO     4 GUIDED   5 LOITER
#   6 RTL         7 CIRCLE    9 LAND      11 DRIFT   13 SPORT   16 POSHOLD
#
# This layout suits a three-position switch driving the six slots in pairs:
# manual, altitude-assisted, then position-hold with RTL on the last notch.
# Adjust to match how your transmitter actually maps its switch -- read the
# live mode name in MAVProxy's prompt while you flick it, and set these to
# match what you want each detent to do.
#
# RTL in at least one position is the point. Without it there is no way to
# hand control back to the aircraft when something goes wrong.
FLTMODE1 0
FLTMODE2 0
FLTMODE3 2
FLTMODE4 2
FLTMODE5 5
FLTMODE6 6
